# a disjunction conjoined with a struct: each alternative is unified with the
# rest, and compared on its own
-- old.cue --
s: {a: int} | {b: int}
-- new.cue --
s: ({a: int} | {b: int} | {c: int}) & {d?: string}
-- out --
unknown
s is now {a: int} | {b: int} | {c: int}, no single alternative of which covers the prior alternative {a: int}; the checker does not combine alternatives (rule unknown-disjunction) @ new.cue:1:1
s is now {a: int} | {b: int} | {c: int}, no single alternative of which covers the prior alternative {b: int}; the checker does not combine alternatives (rule unknown-disjunction) @ new.cue:1:1
